{
  "_comment": [
    "Cross-platform test vectors for matching the bank's USD charges to the",
    "expenses they paid for. The matcher exists twice — apps/web/src/lib/",
    "bank-match.ts and apps/ios/Gastos/Core/BankMatch.swift — and both",
    "must produce the SAME assignment for every case here. Same arrangement as",
    "period-test-vectors.json, and for the same reason: duplicated logic only",
    "stays honest if one file decides what it does.",
    "",
    "Each case lists charges and candidate expenses, the reference rate learned",
    "from history (null = nothing verified yet), and the expected chargeId →",
    "expenseId assignment (null = no suggestion, pick by hand)."
  ],
  "learnRate": [
    {
      "name": "nothing verified yet",
      "expenses": [
        {
          "amountCents": 6390,
          "usdCents": null,
          "verified": false
        },
        {
          "amountCents": 1250,
          "usdCents": null,
          "verified": false
        }
      ],
      "expected": null
    },
    {
      "name": "one verified pair",
      "expenses": [
        {
          "amountCents": 10000,
          "usdCents": 7123,
          "verified": true
        }
      ],
      "expected": 0.7123
    },
    {
      "name": "median, so a mistyped pair cannot drag it",
      "expenses": [
        {
          "amountCents": 10000,
          "usdCents": 7120,
          "verified": true
        },
        {
          "amountCents": 20000,
          "usdCents": 14240,
          "verified": true
        },
        {
          "amountCents": 10000,
          "usdCents": 712,
          "verified": true
        }
      ],
      "expected": 0.712
    },
    {
      "name": "even count averages the middle two",
      "expenses": [
        {
          "amountCents": 10000,
          "usdCents": 7000,
          "verified": true
        },
        {
          "amountCents": 10000,
          "usdCents": 7200,
          "verified": true
        }
      ],
      "expected": 0.71
    },
    {
      "name": "a flag with no figure behind it is not a pair",
      "expenses": [
        {
          "amountCents": 10000,
          "usdCents": null,
          "verified": true
        }
      ],
      "expected": null
    },
    {
      "name": "an estimated pair is left out: its AUD was worked out from this very rate",
      "expenses": [
        {
          "amountCents": 10000,
          "usdCents": 7000,
          "verified": true
        },
        {
          "amountCents": 10000,
          "usdCents": 6000,
          "verified": true,
          "autoEstimated": true
        },
        {
          "amountCents": 10000,
          "usdCents": 6000,
          "verified": true,
          "autoEstimated": true
        }
      ],
      "expected": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "learnRateWindow": {
    "_comment": [
      "The rate is learned from the verified pairs dated in the last windowDays",
      "days up to and including today (household timezone) — the same window",
      "for the open app, the web and the background run, so a charge filed by",
      "any of them is priced at the same rate. Before this the app learned from",
      "the current period plus whichever one was on screen, and the background",
      "run from 45 days: the same charge got a different AUD depending on who",
      "filed it, and browsing last year's period moved today's estimate."
    ],
    "windowDays": 45,
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "a pair from before the window is left out",
        "today": "2026-10-27",
        "expenses": [
          {
            "date": "2026-10-20",
            "amountCents": 10000,
            "usdCents": 7000,
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "date": "2026-09-11",
            "amountCents": 10000,
            "usdCents": 6000,
            "verified": true
          }
        ],
        "expected": 0.7
      },
      {
        "name": "the window's first day counts",
        "today": "2026-10-27",
        "expenses": [
          {
            "date": "2026-09-12",
            "amountCents": 10000,
            "usdCents": 6000,
            "verified": true
          }
        ],
        "expected": 0.6
      },
      {
        "name": "a pair dated after today is left out",
        "today": "2026-10-27",
        "expenses": [
          {
            "date": "2026-10-27",
            "amountCents": 10000,
            "usdCents": 7000,
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "date": "2026-10-28",
            "amountCents": 10000,
            "usdCents": 6000,
            "verified": true
          }
        ],
        "expected": 0.7
      },
      {
        "name": "across a year boundary",
        "today": "2026-01-10",
        "expenses": [
          {
            "date": "2025-11-26",
            "amountCents": 10000,
            "usdCents": 6500,
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "date": "2025-11-25",
            "amountCents": 10000,
            "usdCents": 5000,
            "verified": true
          }
        ],
        "expected": 0.65
      },
      {
        "name": "nothing in the window: no rate, rather than an old one",
        "today": "2026-10-27",
        "expenses": [
          {
            "date": "2026-06-01",
            "amountCents": 10000,
            "usdCents": 7000,
            "verified": true
          }
        ],
        "expected": null
      }
    ]
  },
